==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*surma}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śurma}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|fi|surra|ma|id2=nominal}} (although the original meaning of {{m|fi||surra}} is not found in Finnish). Cognates include {{cog|et|surm}}, {{cog|krl|šurma}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[violent]] [[death]] {{gloss|mainly used of humans}}
#: {{ux|fi|He saivat '''surmansa'''|They got killed|lit=They got '''their deaths'''.}}
# the [[personification]] of sudden [[death]]
#: {{ux|fi|Hän joutui '''surman''' suuhun.|He got killed.|lit=He got into the mouth of '''death'''.}}
# {{lb|fi|legal}} [[killing]], [[voluntary]] [[manslaughter]] under [[mitigating]] circumstances

====Usage notes====
* {{s|law}} "killing" is the ''unofficial'' translation of Finnish penal code used by the Ministry of Justice of Finland. See usage notes under {{m|fi|tappo}}.

